## Summary

`ExchangeClient` can now make the same reads as the Exchange module's `Get-EXO*` cmdlets,
without going through `InvokeCommand`. The point is speed: `Get-Mailbox` returns every
property of every mailbox (338 for one mailbox), while these reads return only the property
set asked for (12 for the audit property set).

There is one method per cmdlet: `mailboxes`, `cas_mailboxes`, `recipients`,
`mailbox_permissions`, `mailbox_folder_permissions`, `mailbox_statistics`,
`mailbox_folder_statistics`, `mobile_device_statistics` and `recipient_permissions`. `get()`
and `iter_get_pages()` read any other path. The request shapes were read from
ExchangeOnlineManagement 3.10.1, since Microsoft documents none of this.

The reads share the plumbing `InvokeCommand` already had: same token, same routing header,
same regional redirect. What differs is that the next page is a GET rather than a re-POST,
and a failed read raises `InvokeCommandError` with the OData error message.

The GDAP tests' read-only guard now also lets through a GET of the whole `Mailbox`
collection, so a live test can read a customer's mailboxes through GDAP. Separately, the
GDAP customer tenant tests now run only when `AZURE_AUTH_TEST_GDAP=1`; before, setting the
customer tenant id alone ran them.

## Type of change

New feature, no breaking changes.

## How it was tested

- Unit tests cover the URL and query each method sends, identity encoding, paging, headers,
  error messages and the regional redirect, for the async and the blocking clients.
- New live tests in `tests/live/test_exchange_rest.py` ran against a sandbox tenant: all
  passed. They read every collection whole and by identity, page at two results a page,
  probe the error shapes, and read as both a signed-in user and an app.
- `ruff`, `mypy` on every platform, and the offline suite pass.

Not yet run live:

- `test_gdap_reads_a_customers_mailboxes_without_prompting` needs a partner tenant sign-in
  with `AZURE_AUTH_TEST_GDAP=1` and a customer tenant id. It settles which routing header a
  customer tenant's GET endpoint accepts under GDAP.
- The mobile device lookup by device identity: the sandbox user has no devices.
